# REQUIRES: cuda
# The stack of `mdir run` does not grow with the rows that a run writes
# (#305) on a GPU, in double and mixed precision, as stack-rows.test has it
# for the CPU. On a GPU the rows never grew the stack: the lowering releases
# the stack of an iteration of a loop of the host where the iteration ends
# (`releaseStack`), since the arguments of its launches are on the stack as
# well. The test keeps that: the runs end under the limit, and an allocation
# of the lowered module outside the first block of its function stands with
# a `stacksave`.
# RUN: rm -rf %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/stack_rows.py mdir %t/double GPU DOUBLE | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/stack_rows.py mdir %t/mixed GPU MIXED | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the energies alone: 131072 rows under a stack of 2 MiB {{.*}}: status 0, the last rows at 131072: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the energies alone: the lowered module has no allocation of the stack outside the first block of a function, or releases the stack of an iteration: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: observe, 6 columns: 131072 rows under a stack of 2 MiB (48 bytes a row taken in the loop would be 3.0 of it): status 0, the last rows at 131072, 131072: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: observe, 6 columns: the lowered module has no allocation of the stack outside the first block of a function, or releases the stack of an iteration: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: pull, 2 terms over two centers: 43690 rows under a stack of 2 MiB (144 bytes a row taken in the loop would be 3.0 of it): status 0, the last rows at 43690, 43690: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: pull, 2 terms over two centers: the lowered module has no allocation of the stack outside the first block of a function, or releases the stack of an iteration: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: free energy, 11 states: 32768 rows under a stack of 2 MiB (192 bytes a row taken in the loop would be 3.0 of it): status 0, the last rows at 32768, 32768: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: free energy, 11 states: the lowered module has no allocation of the stack outside the first block of a function, or releases the stack of an iteration: True
# CHECK: stack rows passed
